  "scope": "Fixed-view local task, independent station placement/occlusion and controlled live lifecycle. No seamless repeat, direction continuity, moving sole contact or hidden geometry approval.",
  "checks": {
    "identity-and-scale": "All eight native and layered poses retain the same bald stocky smith, dark forked brass-bound beard, cream sleeves, leather apron, olive trousers and boots. Source-bound520px standing basis and root320/616 match the existing anvil actor. Actual in-game standing registration is reviewed at the fixed station; other views and translating contacts excluded.",
    "station-and-foot-contact": "The independent anvil/stump stays fixed across all eight poses and after cancellation/day completion. Visible standing boots keep the local base; the nearer supporting region is partially occluded by the stump, with no claim for hidden geometry. Actor has no painted anvil. The raised hand/tool remains above the station, so no foreground copy is needed.",
    "hand-and-tool-contact": "Same small steel/wood tool stays in the raised gripping hand through chest hold0/1, lift2/3, wrist rotation4/5 and lower6/7. Opposite empty arm remains connected. This is inspection, not striking or metallurgical workpiece replacement.",
    "prop-continuity": "One independent anvil remains at the forge, with no duplicate anvil or carried spare hammer. The same held tool remains present from0 through7; body and props do not switch direction during the finite task.",
    "completion-and-reset": "Exact live renderer and authored durations expose0-7, complete once, hold7 for5000ms and reset only on explicit assignment/day change. A day chooses one operation; completion does not trigger another operation. Repair routing walks naturally to its distinct bench. Renderer never grants inventory or building rewards; existing day resolution retains economic ownership."
  },
